snapshot-wiki (0.1.7) unstable; urgency=low

  * Quiet network defaults: a Wi-Fi section. wpasupplicant is now on the
    image, so NetworkManager joins Wi-Fi and wired 802.1X networks, and
    NetworkManager's Wi-Fi switch ships off: adapters stay unavailable and
    send no probe requests until the operator turns Wi-Fi on (network icon,
    or nmcli radio wifi on). The switch is also an rfkill soft block; once
    on, NetworkManager scans with a random MAC address.
  * airodump-ng: monitor mode next to the Wi-Fi switch. Unblock only the
    survey adapter with rfkill and leave the switch off; airmon-ng check now
    lists NetworkManager and wpa_supplicant, and check kill also drops the
    wired connections. The quick start gains the rfkill steps. The wireless
    survey playbook and the rules of engagement say the same.
  * Live session and install: Secure Boot works on the live ISO and on
    installed systems (shim and signed GRUB in EFI/SnapshOT and at the
    removable media path EFI/BOOT), with the kernel lockdown it brings;
    the live session points at the Wi-Fi switch. Architectures: the
    installed bootloader row and a Secure Boot row.
  * flashrom: with Secure Boot on, lockdown stops the internal programmer;
    external programmers are unaffected.

